<title>USA: Nasdaq delists Princeton America.</title>
<headline>Nasdaq delists Princeton America.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Nasdaq Stock Market said on Monday that it has delisted shares of Princeton America Corp after the company's chairman, Dale Eyman, was cited in a recent stock fraud case.</p>
<p>Eyman was charged with participating in a scheme to bribe a stockbroker to buy company shares in the open market, the Nasdaq said.</p>
<p>Nasdaq said Princeton America was the third Nasdaq company in the fraud case brought in the U.S. Federal District Court for the Southern District of New York to be delisted from the market.  </p>
<p>Nasdaq said a hearing panel recommended the delisting on November 14, after a hearing.</p>
<p>Earlier this month Cam-Net Communications Network Inc and Alpha Solarco Inc were delisted on the Nasdaq, after being named in the fraud case.</p>
